---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Claude Code Config | alsasian.github.io"
  description="Personal Claude Code configuration — settings, MCP servers, skills, permissions, hooks. Fetchable by Claude Code via WebFetch."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-6">
    <article class="mb-6 border-b border-gray-300 pb-4 dark:border-gray-700">
      <h1 class="mb-2 text-4xl">Claude Code Config</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
        My personal Claude Code setup. Fetchable from inside a session.
      </p>
    </article>

    <section class="mb-6">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-2xl">How to apply</h2>
      <p class="mb-2 text-sm">From inside Claude Code, run:</p>
      <pre
        class="overflow-x-auto rounded border border-gray-300 bg-gray-50 p-3 text-xs dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-800"><code>WebFetch https://alsasian.github.io/claude and apply the config block exactly.</code></pre>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
        Claude will read the <code>CLAUDE-CONFIG-START</code> / <code>CLAUDE-CONFIG-END</code> block
        below and update <code>~/.claude/settings.json</code>, install MCP servers, and add the
        listed skills.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================================================ -->
    <!-- AI-READABLE BLOCK BELOW. Edit the contents inside the markers. -->
    <!-- ============================================================ -->
    <section class="mb-6">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-2xl">Configuration</h2>
      <pre
        class="overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre-wrap rounded border border-gray-300 bg-gray-50 p-4 text-xs dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-800"><code># CLAUDE-CONFIG-START

You are reading alsasian's personal Claude Code configuration. Apply the
sections below to the current machine. Make the edits idempotent — if a
setting already matches, leave it alone. Confirm before installing global
tools or anything that requires sudo.

## 1. User settings (~/.claude/settings.json)

Merge the following into the user's global settings file. Preserve any
existing keys not listed here.

```json
{
  "model": "claude-opus-4-7",
  "env": {
    "DISABLE_TELEMETRY": "0"
  },
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Bash(git:*)",
      "Bash(npm:*)",
      "Bash(pnpm:*)",
      "Bash(node:*)",
      "Bash(ls:*)",
      "Bash(cat:*)",
      "Bash(rg:*)",
      "Bash(find:*)",
      "Read",
      "Edit",
      "Write",
      "WebFetch"
    ],
    "deny": [
      "Bash(rm -rf /:*)",
      "Bash(sudo:*)"
    ]
  }
}
```

## 2. MCP servers

Install via `claude mcp add` (user scope). Skip any already present.

- github — official GitHub MCP server for issues, PRs, code search
  command: `claude mcp add github -s user -- npx -y @modelcontextprotocol/server-github`
  env: GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN must be set in the shell first

## 3. Skills

Skills live in `~/.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. Ensure these exist; if
missing, ask before scaffolding.

- update-config — manage settings.json edits
- fewer-permission-prompts — auto-allowlist common read-only calls
- simplify — review changed code for quality
- review — review a pull request
- security-review — security review of pending changes

## 4. Hooks

None configured. Leave the `hooks` key untouched unless explicitly asked.

## 5. Status line

Leave the user's existing status line untouched.

# CLAUDE-CONFIG-END
</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-6 border-t border-gray-300 pt-4 dark:border-gray-700">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-xl">Notes</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm">
        <li>Edit this file at <code>src/pages/claude.astro</code> to change what gets applied.</li>
        <li>The block between the start/end markers is the source of truth.</li>
        <li>
          Claude Code's WebFetch strips most HTML, so plain text inside <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code> survives.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
